@startuml customer-journey
title A2. Sign-in, Ordering and Access Control
autonumber 1 "<b>00</b>"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Customer / Admin" as user #E0F2FE
participant "Browser\nReact" as ui #E0F2FE
participant "Nginx\n/api proxy" as proxy #E0F2FE
participant "Spring Security\nSession + CSRF + roles" as security #DCFCE7
participant "Controllers / Services" as api #DCFCE7
database "PostgreSQL\nvia JPA repositories" as db #FEF3C7

== Sign in: one form for all roles ==
user -> ui : Enter email and password on /login
ui -> proxy : GET /api/v1/auth/csrf
proxy -> security : Retrieve session-bound CSRF token
security --> ui : Token through Nginx; session cookie
ui -> proxy : POST /api/v1/auth/login\nCredentials + cookie + CSRF header
proxy -> security : Validate CSRF; dispatch login
security -> api : Authenticate local credentials
api -> db : Look up account; verify BCrypt hash in backend
db --> api : Account with role
api --> ui : Save authenticated session; return account\n(response via Nginx)
alt ADMIN account
  ui --> user : Navigate to /admin
else CUSTOMER account
  ui --> user : Navigate to coffee board /
end

== Place an order: backend owns price and identity ==
user -> ui : Select coffee and quantity
ui -> proxy : GET CSRF token; then POST /api/v1/orders\nBody: coffeeId and quantity, not price or customerId
proxy -> security : Forward session cookie and CSRF header
security -> api : Allow authenticated request\nResolve customer from authenticated principal
api -> db : Read available coffee and current unit price
db --> api : Coffee data
api -> api : Calculate total = stored unit price x quantity
api -> db : Save account ownership, coffee name/price snapshot,\nquantity, total and creation timestamp
db --> api : Saved order
api --> ui : 201 Created with authoritative total
ui --> user : Display confirmation

== Read orders / enforce role boundaries ==
ui -> proxy : GET /api/v1/orders (customer)\nor GET /api/v1/admin/orders (admin workspace)
proxy -> security : Authorize session and route
alt Allowed
  security -> api : Personal list: filter by principal's account ID\nAdmin list: require ADMIN role
  api -> db : Query authorized order scope
  db --> api : Matching orders
  api --> ui : Order history
else Missing session / insufficient role
  security --> ui : 401 / 403; no protected data returned
end

note over security, api #FEE2E2
  Catalog POST / PUT / DELETE also require ADMIN.
  Browser route guards are UX only; the API enforces authorization.
end note
legend bottom
  Blue: user interface and delivery | Green: trusted backend | Amber: data
  Numbered messages show the normal local-account flow.
  Keycloak is not integrated yet. Proxy return hops are condensed for readability.
endlegend
@enduml